From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone: Wi-Fi powered in suspend

rtw88's SDIO suspend asks the host to keep the card powered
(MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER) and fails when it cannot, which aborts system
suspend: with Wi-Fi bound, deep sleep never started ("Failed to host PM
flag MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER", -EINVAL). Its resume does nothing, so a card
that lost power does not come back either.

As in megi's tree (orange-pi-7.3): keep the card powered, and describe
the chip's wake line, WL_WAKE_AP on PL3. PL is the R_PIO port, which can
wake the A64 from Crust's deep sleep, for WoWLAN.

Not solved yet: a suspend soon after boot, likely while Wi-Fi is still
associating, sometimes hangs the phone (s2idle and deep alike, also with
pm_test=core). With Wi-Fi off it does not; later in a boot, suspend and
resume with Wi-Fi associated work.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
@@ -394,10 +394,13 @@
 	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_dldo4>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
 	non-removable;
+	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	status = "okay";

 	rtl8723cs: wifi@1 {
 		reg = <1>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&r_pio>;
+		interrupts = <0 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>; /* PL3, WL_WAKE_AP */
 	};
 };

